commit 3e63b5fc170e12611ec46a11cd57975d7356c7df
Author: ai.teammate <agent.ai.native@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 26 05:19:00 2026 +0200

    fix(1886): require implies its granularity + payload-level enforcement (AC5, threads 6-10)

    - require: word/segment now IMPLIES the demanded granularity in the
      outbound request when granularities is unset (_requestedGranularities):
      the demanded level is always asked for, so endpoints that honor
      timestamp_granularities actually deliver it.
    - _enforceRequirementsOnPayload no longer gates on the requested set: the
      requirement is enforced against the payload REGARDLESS of what was
      requested — require: word + empty granularities + a segments-only 200 is
      now a hard actionable error, never success-with-no-warning (bot probe
      case). The word-timings-unsupported warning stays request-gated.
    - Thread 7 (decisive semantics): require: segment demands SEGMENTS
      specifically; a words-only payload does NOT satisfy it (segments carry
      the text slices downstream consumers — e.g. SRT export — need). Locked
      by a test.
    - Thread 8: non-list segments/words payload shapes degrade with a
      machine-readable warning instead of a raw cast crash (_asListOrWarn,
      growable warnings copy); +1 test.
    - Thread 9: TranscribeAudioConfig.sessionId field dropped — one seam (the
      transcribeAudioTool sessionId parameter hosts wire).
    - Thread 10: rebutted with evidence — bin/fah_runapp.dart boots AgentCli
      (line 1463), whose services wiring (agent_cli.dart) already passes
      transcribeSessionId: () => _session?.cachedId; runapp sidecars are
      session-scoped, not sessionless.

    New tests: implied word request on the wire (empty granularities),
    require:word + empty granularities + segments-only 200 -> hard error,
    words-only payload vs require:segment -> hard error, non-list nested
    shapes. 1190 tests green; local CRAP: worst in touched files 10.10,
    _transcribeVerbose 9.04, _enforceRequirementsOnPayload 9.00.

